      "writtenOn": "2025-01-16T14:39:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for the clarification. You are correct that in the specific case where the buffer size is 100 and the string \"Unknown state\" (including the null-terminator) fits comfortably.\n\nHowever the use of sizeof(buf) - 1 is intended as a safety measure for all scenarios, including cases where the buffer size and string length might not be so neatly aligned. The purpose of reserving one byte for the null-terminator is to ensure that:\n\n1. If the buffer size were smaller than the string length (including the null-terminator) this would prevent writing past the buffer’s boundary.\n2. The null-terminator would still be explicitly set preventing potential undefined behavior from missing or incorrect string termination.\n\nSo while the current case may seem safe the practice of using sizeof(buf) - 1 helps maintain a more general, robust approach to handling buffers, ensuring that null-termination is properly managed in all situations.",
      "parentUuid": "61adcdb9_5472e39c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 7,
        "endChar": 72
      },
